#
# Damage tracking in the legacy-API (libwpe) build, off until it is
# measured on the phones: WEBKIT_DAMAGE_COMPOSITING=1 turns it on.
#
# WTF defines ENABLE_DAMAGE_TRACKING only with ENABLE(WPE_PLATFORM) or on
# GTK, so in ours (WPEPlatform off) all of it was compiled out, Atlantic's
# WEBKIT_DAMAGE_COMPOSITING switch (webkit-damage-limited-composite-env)
# with it, and patch 0001 throttles offscreen animations instead. Turning
# WPEPlatform on for it would add the libWPEPlatform library and its
# dependencies (epoxy, GIO and xkbcommon; the DRM backend libinput, udev
# and GBM, the Wayland one wayland and wayland-protocols; both can be
# switched off, ENABLE_WPE_PLATFORM_DRM/WAYLAND/HEADLESS) and every
# WPEPlatform code path, for nothing Pacific uses. Nothing under
# ENABLE(DAMAGE_TRACKING) needs WPEPlatform: the damage classes, the Skia
# and TextureMapper compositors, LayerTreeHost, ThreadedCompositor and
# AcceleratedSurface's tracker are the same code for every target. So it
# is defined for PLATFORM(WPE) too.
#
# Two things change with it:
#
# - Defaults. WebKit's preferences turn damage propagation, unified
#   regions and damage-limited compositing on for GTK and WPE once the
#   feature is compiled in. Here they stay off unless WPEPlatform is on, so
#   the engine composites as before; Atlantic's env vars
#   (WEBKIT_DAMAGE_COMPOSITING=1, WEBKIT_DAMAGE_UNIFY,
#   WEBKIT_DAMAGE_USE_FOR_COMPOSITING) turn it on for A/B tests.
#
# - Buffer age. The tracker assumes a target holds the frame last presented
#   on it: true of the shareable-buffer swap chains (one target per
#   buffer), not of the WPEBackend's EGL window, one target for every
#   buffer its EGL rotates, each holding whatever frame it last held (two
#   or three frames back with libhybris). Drawing only the last frame's
#   damage into it would leave older frames' pixels on screen. The tracker
#   now keeps what the last four frames presented to it changed and, before
#   each frame, sets the target's record from EGL_EXT_buffer_age: the
#   frames since that buffer was shown; a full repaint when the age is
#   unknown (no extension, or 0) or older than the history.
#
# Untested: the engine has not been built with it (Atlantic's patches
# under ENABLE(DAMAGE_TRACKING) were never compiled before either). Check
# EGL_EXT_buffer_age in device-check.sh's EGL extensions first.
#
